  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 4.46,
      "end": 10.46,
      "text": "On 275 and 285 and Stereo VHS, this is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.46,
      "end": 36.65,
      "text": "Good evening, Tommy Vance is on holiday, so for the next two weeks on The Rock Show, it's me, Geoff Barton. I'm going to enjoy myself, I hope you will too.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.65,
      "end": 65.78,
      "text": "On tonight's show we have Motley Crue, Sweet, Stars, Diamondhead, Blue Cheer, a session from Fist, archive tracks from Humble Pie, and who knows, maybe the odd track from Kiss along the way.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.78,
      "end": 76.04,
      "text": "But we start with a band called Stray Dog and Tramp, how it is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.34,
      "end": 78.08,
      "text": "So clunk, click, we're on our way.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.08,
      "end": 180.52,
      "text": "My command, to know they wanna hold me",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.52,
      "end": 184.58,
      "text": "Gives the power of the sun, yes I know",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 184.58,
      "end": 193.78,
      "text": "I just keep right on floatin', got no blues that I can see",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 193.78,
      "end": 198.0,
      "text": "Cause nothing can tame my...",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.0,
      "end": 202.8,
      "text": "Stray Dog there and Tramp, how it is.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 470.14,
      "end": 473.2,
      "text": "That was from their debut album, released back in 1973.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 473.2,
      "end": 477.82,
      "text": "Stray Dog, you may remember, were on Emerson Lake & Palmer's old Manticore label",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 477.82,
      "end": 480.7,
      "text": "Their guitarist was a guy called Snuffy Walden",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 480.7,
      "end": 483.46,
      "text": "And I don't know, I think they were a much underrated band",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 483.46,
      "end": 485.44,
      "text": "They deserved to do much better than they did",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 485.44,
      "end": 488.7,
      "text": "Right, Jeff Barton for Tommy Vance",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 488.7,
      "end": 492.34,
      "text": "And Ian Gillan has released a single from his new album Magic",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 492.34,
      "end": 493.9,
      "text": "This is Long Gone",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 493.9,
      "end": 501.1,
      "text": "And Long Gone out as a single from his new album Magic",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 501.1,
      "end": 731.53,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 731.53,
      "end": 735.23,
      "text": "I'm looking forward to seeing him on his new UK tour",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 735.23,
      "end": 738.55,
      "text": "On the paper, we've just received some outrageous pictures",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 738.55,
      "end": 741.83,
      "text": "of some sort of stage presentation Ian Gillan's going to be putting on.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 742.37,
      "end": 744.47,
      "text": "He's going around daubed in war paint",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 744.47,
      "end": 747.29,
      "text": "and surrounded by three ladies called the Cucumbers,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 747.87,
      "end": 752.01,
      "text": "who I can only describe as refugees from a pornographic Beatrix Potter novel.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 752.59,
      "end": 754.49,
      "text": "Well, we'll wait and see what that's like.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 754.85,
      "end": 758.65,
      "text": "And coming up next, the first track from our session band, Fist.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 758.99,
      "end": 759.83,
      "text": "This is Lucy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 760.27,
      "end": 766.27,
      "text": "Lucy there from our session group, North East Band, Fist.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 952.14,
      "end": 955.6,
      "text": "Right, and now a track from one of my favourite bands of all time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 956.02,
      "end": 958.12,
      "text": "This is an American group called Stars,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 958.5,
      "end": 962.0,
      "text": "and rock not once, not twice, but six times.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1156.46,
      "end": 1158.86,
      "text": "Stars there, and a track from their second album,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1159.02,
      "end": 1160.94,
      "text": "Violation, rock six times.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1161.48,
      "end": 1163.92,
      "text": "Some great American pop metal there, I think.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1164.58,
      "end": 1166.74,
      "text": "Stars, of course, are no longer together,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1166.94,
      "end": 1170.02,
      "text": "but their old lead singer, a guy called Michael Lee Smith,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1170.48,
      "end": 1172.6,
      "text": "has just formed a new band called The Hellcats.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1173.28,
      "end": 1176.48,
      "text": "This is a track from, well, it's not quite an album",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1176.48,
      "end": 1178.44,
      "text": "and it's not quite a single either.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1178.5,
      "end": 1181.64,
      "text": "It's a sort of six-track taster thing out on import",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1181.64,
      "end": 1183.3,
      "text": "from the band Hellcats.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1183.3,
      "end": 1187.74,
      "text": "And this song has got the rather suggestive title of",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1187.74,
      "end": 1188.8,
      "text": "You Make It Swell.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1189.24,
      "end": 1193.44,
      "text": "You Make It Swell there from Stars,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1193.44,
      "end": 1400.43,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1400.43,
      "end": 1401.91,
      "text": "well, the new Stars, should I say,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1402.31,
      "end": 1403.97,
      "text": "American band the Hellcats.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1404.47,
      "end": 1407.59,
      "text": "Right, that's out on import, as I said,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1407.69,
      "end": 1409.39,
      "text": "on the Radio Records label",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1409.39,
      "end": 1410.91,
      "text": "and well worth checking out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1410.97,
      "end": 1413.29,
      "text": "It cost me the princely sum of £6.50,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1413.45,
      "end": 1415.41,
      "text": "which is quite a lot for about five tracks,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1415.57,
      "end": 1417.65,
      "text": "but I think it's worth it in the end.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1418.27,
      "end": 1423.07,
      "text": "OK, Geoff the Barton speaking on behalf of the Holidaying Thomas the Vance,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1423.07,
      "end": 1427.57,
      "text": "and right now, the first tracks from our archive band, Humble Pie.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1427.77,
      "end": 1430.59,
      "text": "So, without further ado, over to you, Brian Matthew.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1430.95,
      "end": 1433.31,
      "text": "And here's our latest supergroup, Humble Pie,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1433.59,
      "end": 1436.23,
      "text": "with small-faced Stephen Marriott, Peter Frampton of The Herd",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1436.23,
      "end": 1438.03,
      "text": "and Greg Ridley from Spooky 2.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1438.33,
      "end": 1439.15,
      "text": "Let's hear it, fellas!",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1439.39,
      "end": 1443.11,
      "text": "There she is again, steppin' out of her limo",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1443.11,
      "end": 1447.31,
      "text": "There somewhere's got my soul to take",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1447.31,
      "end": 1732.97,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1732.97,
      "end": 1736.21,
      "text": "I took one flower so nobody's gonna weep",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1736.21,
      "end": 1738.15,
      "text": "Just feel I sit out low",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1738.15,
      "end": 1739.25,
      "text": "Shakey Jake",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1739.25,
      "end": 1745.01,
      "text": "I ain't just comin' out here",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1745.01,
      "end": 1751.86,
      "text": "Shakey Jake",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1751.86,
      "end": 1757.26,
      "text": "Sure, Woody Woody never had it so good there.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1935.52,
      "end": 1939.1,
      "text": "From 1969 there, three brilliant tracks from Humble Pie.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1939.5,
      "end": 1941.56,
      "text": "The first was Natural Born Boogie,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1942.0,
      "end": 1944.78,
      "text": "second Shakey Jake and third Heartbeat there.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1945.26,
      "end": 1946.92,
      "text": "We'll be hearing more from Humble Pie later,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1947.26,
      "end": 1949.04,
      "text": "but right now we're coming bang up to date",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1949.04,
      "end": 1952.66,
      "text": "with Los Angeles glam metal band Motley Crue.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1953.2,
      "end": 1956.06,
      "text": "So slip on your spandex pants and stiletto heels.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1956.46,
      "end": 1960.06,
      "text": "This is Livewire, Motley Crue there,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2156.02,
      "end": 2158.58,
      "text": "and a track from their debut album Too Fast for Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2158.96,
      "end": 2163.18,
      "text": "That was from their Elektra version of that particular album,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2163.52,
      "end": 2165.1,
      "text": "remixed by Roy Thomas Baker.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2165.8,
      "end": 2169.54,
      "text": "If you're in the possession of their original version of that",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2169.54,
      "end": 2172.34,
      "text": "on their own independent leather records labelled,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2172.42,
      "end": 2175.86,
      "text": "and I think you'll probably get a bit of a collector's item there.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2175.92,
      "end": 2178.64,
      "text": "Hang on to it. It could be worth a few bob in the future.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2179.2,
      "end": 2183.1,
      "text": "Right, from modern-day glam metal to a touch of the old stuff.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2183.44,
      "end": 2185.12,
      "text": "This is Sweet and Windy City.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2186.2,
      "end": 2191.6,
      "text": "And a track from their off-the-record album, Windy City.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2635.98,
      "end": 2638.24,
      "text": "That was especially for a guy called Bob Henry",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2638.24,
      "end": 2640.6,
      "text": "of James Street Macduff in Banffshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2641.1,
      "end": 2642.84,
      "text": "He's written in requesting a dedication",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2642.84,
      "end": 2645.64,
      "text": "for the Banff Scouts and Venture Scouts.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2645.78,
      "end": 2648.44,
      "text": "apparently the most mental scout group in Britain.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2649.08,
      "end": 2654.84,
      "text": "So he also asked for mentions for Smarty, Dick, Ewan, Dingwall, Man of Steel,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2655.22,
      "end": 2656.66,
      "text": "and In Is The Mad Butcher.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2656.96,
      "end": 2657.74,
      "text": "So there you go, Bob.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2658.18,
      "end": 2661.16,
      "text": "Right, second track now from our session band Fist.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2661.42,
      "end": 2662.54,
      "text": "This is called Vamp.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2664.78,
      "end": 2671.98,
      "text": "Powerful stuff there from our session band Fist, and that was Vamp.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2888.83,
      "end": 2891.51,
      "text": "Right, Jeff Barton for Tommy Vance and Diamond Head",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2891.51,
      "end": 2895.27,
      "text": "have finally got their first album out for their MCA label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2895.75,
      "end": 2900.19,
      "text": "This is perhaps their best-loved track, the chilling Am I Evil?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2900.87,
      "end": 2908.67,
      "text": "Yes, more doomy riffs than the first six dozen Black Sabbath albums there.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3347.5,
      "end": 3353.08,
      "text": "Diamondhead and Am I Evil from their debut MCA album Living on Borrowed Time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3353.52,
      "end": 3355.92,
      "text": "I must admit that's the first time I've heard this particular version",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3355.92,
      "end": 3359.38,
      "text": "and I don't know, I feel a bit lukewarm about it actually.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3359.38,
      "end": 3361.74,
      "text": "I'm not convinced also that",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3361.74,
      "end": 3363.88,
      "text": "Diamondhead know quite what they're letting themselves",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3363.88,
      "end": 3365.82,
      "text": "in for, having Twisted Sister supporting",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3365.82,
      "end": 3367.04,
      "text": "them on their British tour",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3367.04,
      "end": 3368.76,
      "text": "well we shall see",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3368.76,
      "end": 3371.98,
      "text": "going over the seas now to Canada",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3371.98,
      "end": 3373.84,
      "text": "a country that seems",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3373.84,
      "end": 3375.94,
      "text": "to have an uncanny knack of producing",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3375.94,
      "end": 3376.82,
      "text": "good rock bands",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3376.82,
      "end": 3379.6,
      "text": "people like Rush obviously and Backman Turner",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3379.6,
      "end": 3381.82,
      "text": "Overdrive and lesser known",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3381.82,
      "end": 3383.98,
      "text": "people as well like the Max Webster band",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3383.98,
      "end": 3385.36,
      "text": "and even a group called Zon",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3385.36,
      "end": 3386.96,
      "text": "I remember from a few years back",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3386.96,
      "end": 3389.44,
      "text": "This group is the latest in a long line",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3389.44,
      "end": 3390.56,
      "text": "They're called Coney Hatch",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3390.56,
      "end": 3392.94,
      "text": "And continuing with the theme of evil",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3392.94,
      "end": 3394.32,
      "text": "This is Devil's Deck",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3394.32,
      "end": 3397.32,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3397.32,
      "end": 4480.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4480.79,
      "end": 4484.87,
      "text": "Compiled by Doug Pym of Broccoli London SE4",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4484.87,
      "end": 4488.47,
      "text": "Right, can you fathom the link between those three tracks?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4488.47,
      "end": 4489.55,
      "text": "If you think you can",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4489.55,
      "end": 4492.17,
      "text": "Then send your entries to the Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4492.17,
      "end": 4496.21,
      "text": "Radio 1, BBC, London, W1A4WW",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4496.21,
      "end": 4500.19,
      "text": "And don't forget to compile a connection of your own",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4500.19,
      "end": 4505.11,
      "text": "uh apparently quite a lot you did this week and it's quite important uh because uh you will not",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4505.11,
      "end": 4509.41,
      "text": "be considered for uh for the competition if you don't compile a connection of your own so don't",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4509.41,
      "end": 4518.59,
      "text": "forget that okay now graham bonnet may not be in the michael shenker group anymore but he's still",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4518.59,
      "end": 4528.19,
      "text": "on the new lp this is assault attack assault attack there from the michael shenker group",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4780.52,
      "end": 4785.28,
      "text": "featuring graham bonnet as i said who put in a very powerful vocal performance there and",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4785.28,
      "end": 4787.82,
      "text": "displayed none of the rather dubious qualities",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4787.82,
      "end": 4791.28,
      "text": "that got him thrown out of the group at Sheffield Polytechnic",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4791.28,
      "end": 4794.42,
      "text": "just prior to the Michael Schenker Group's reading appearance.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4794.94,
      "end": 4796.36,
      "text": "In fact, something interesting here,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4796.6,
      "end": 4800.18,
      "text": "one of our writers has just done an interview with Michael Schenker for the paper,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4800.86,
      "end": 4805.62,
      "text": "and Michael says in the interview that part of the problem with Graham Bonnet",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4805.62,
      "end": 4807.46,
      "text": "is in fact that he is an epileptic,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4807.82,
      "end": 4811.86,
      "text": "and, you know, he's not all that stable on stage,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4812.0,
      "end": 4815.08,
      "text": "and, you know, he threw a bit of a wobbler at Sheffield,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4815.08,
      "end": 4818.12,
      "text": "and his epilepsy was something to do with it, apparently.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4818.34,
      "end": 4822.54,
      "text": "So something interesting that will be revealed in a few weeks' time anyway, in full.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4823.02,
      "end": 4826.48,
      "text": "Right, another track now from our session band Fist.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4826.64,
      "end": 4827.78,
      "text": "This is The Wanderer.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4828.16,
      "end": 4835.36,
      "text": "The Wanderer there from North East band Fist, our session band tonight.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4990.15,
      "end": 4993.43,
      "text": "Right, I've got a letter in front of me from a guy called Colin Stirrat",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4993.43,
      "end": 4996.71,
      "text": "of Ambrose Rive, Deadridge in Livington.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4997.23,
      "end": 5000.73,
      "text": "And he's rather critical of a track Tommy played a couple of weeks ago,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5000.73,
      "end": 5002.93,
      "text": "a track from a band called Clove and Hoof",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5002.93,
      "end": 5005.19,
      "text": "I'll just read a little bit of the letter",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5005.19,
      "end": 5006.81,
      "text": "that Colin wrote here, he says",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5006.81,
      "end": 5008.91,
      "text": "I'd rather not experience",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5008.91,
      "end": 5011.17,
      "text": "some one string, one note rabble",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5011.17,
      "end": 5012.95,
      "text": "of a group called Clove and Hoof",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5012.95,
      "end": 5015.23,
      "text": "well, especially for you Colin",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5015.23,
      "end": 5017.05,
      "text": "here is Clove and Hoof and a track",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5017.05,
      "end": 5018.51,
      "text": "from their 12 inch EP",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5018.51,
      "end": 5020.27,
      "text": "The Gates of Gehenna",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5020.27,
      "end": 5023.87,
      "text": "the mysterious realm of Warsaw there",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5023.87,
      "end": 5390.37,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5390.37,
      "end": 5392.41,
      "text": "the cataclysmic Clove and Hoof",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5392.41,
      "end": 5393.57,
      "text": "and The Gates of Gehenna",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5393.57,
      "end": 5396.45,
      "text": "Geoff Barton for Tommy Vance and back to our archive",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5396.45,
      "end": 5398.47,
      "text": "session now. This is Humble Pie",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5398.47,
      "end": 5400.27,
      "text": "visiting Crufts way back in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5400.27,
      "end": 5402.25,
      "text": "1971 with The Big Black",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5402.25,
      "end": 5402.73,
      "text": "Dog.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5403.31,
      "end": 5417.4,
      "text": "I was on my way. You're gonna do a cheeto.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5418.46,
      "end": 5419.58,
      "text": "Well, I",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5419.58,
      "end": 5422.58,
      "text": "jumped back. Two excellent archive",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5939.54,
      "end": 5940.98,
      "text": "tracks here from Humble Pie.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5941.52,
      "end": 5943.46,
      "text": "That was called Rolling Stone and before",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5943.46,
      "end": 5945.32,
      "text": "that, The Big Black Dog.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5945.88,
      "end": 5947.54,
      "text": "Right, I've got a letter here from",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5947.54,
      "end": 5949.16,
      "text": "a guy called Andy Fisher",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5949.16,
      "end": 5951.4,
      "text": "who lives at 9, the Ridgeway",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5951.4,
      "end": 5952.74,
      "text": "Stanmore in Middlesex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5953.28,
      "end": 5955.5,
      "text": "He goes to the same school as producer Tony",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5955.5,
      "end": 5961.7,
      "text": "Wilson did way back in the Dark Ages. The school is Mill Hill School, and Andy also",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5961.7,
      "end": 5969.34,
      "text": "wants mentions for Chris Dawson, Andy, I'm an art student, Dixon, and Henry Pyromaniac",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5969.34,
      "end": 5974.96,
      "text": "Mitchell, obviously a man after my own heart. For you lot, this is Samson and Life on the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5974.96,
      "end": 5986.36,
      "text": "Run. Samson there and Life on the Run. I had to fade it a little early there because I've",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6183.65,
      "end": 6189.55,
      "text": "save the best tracks till last first off as promised in the radio times we go back to 1967",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6189.55,
      "end": 6194.61,
      "text": "and the earliest days of heavy metal this is a brilliant band called blue cheer",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6194.61,
      "end": 6198.29,
      "text": "and an outrageous version of eddie cochran's summertime blues",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6198.29,
      "end": 6207.89,
      "text": "mind-blowing stuff there from blue cheer and uh one of my favorite albums of all time",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6432.1,
      "end": 6437.7,
      "text": "vincibus eruptum and it was uh summertime blues as i say something from 67 and the very very",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6437.7,
      "end": 6444.38,
      "text": "earliest days of heavy metal okay before we get to the highlight of the show um the final track",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6444.38,
      "end": 6453.38,
      "text": "from our session band fist it's uh something called dog soldier powerful stuff there from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6616.94,
      "end": 6623.64,
      "text": "our session band fist final track from them dog soldier that was called right it had to happen",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6623.64,
      "end": 6629.94,
      "text": "um final track of the evening is of course from kiss and it's something from well possibly my",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6629.94,
      "end": 6631.9,
      "text": "favourite album of all time, certainly the greatest",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6631.9,
      "end": 6633.94,
      "text": "live album of all time, a live",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6633.94,
      "end": 6635.8,
      "text": "one, and Kiss,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6635.96,
      "end": 6637.26,
      "text": "those make-up demons,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6637.84,
      "end": 6639.64,
      "text": "Black Diamond, here we go.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}